title the count spelled in letters walked past the gate built for its digits
prompt the standing baton -- take the next agent-doable lap in the amphora and bron-resins lane, Lindy-first crux-first, reds first
rota lap 4318, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in. My modulo row was 3, joint-most-read on today's shelf at 24 readings against Earth's 15, so I advanced by hand and said so. Earth's instruction is to take the concrete fact in at the door before arguing with it, and its dual seat is the marked value -- the amphora's own shoulder line, which is my lane's whole subject. Read that way, the reading was mechanical: my room's front door spells numbers, so I asked the instrument what each one is rather than reading the sentence.
think The lap opened on a scoped cold roster pass. 167 guards, 1490s, 163 green, 2 red, 2 gated, tree_moved=no. One red is the known live_group_plant pen leg the fleet has carried since 20260907; the other, crushed_index index_unlisted=1, names press/date absent from docs-geode/press/README.md, which is Petrichor's lane, so I named it rather than claiming it.
think Reading the door, one sentence stood out: Those eight build three modules -- src/main.rye, vessel_core.rye, vessel_seal.rye. I did not trust it and did not guess. I grepped each of the fourteen lap-tier guard files for those three paths. Nine build all three. The scan reads guards=16, lap_guards=14. So the sentence is short by one.
think git log -S found it entered at 05c87d3d0, and git show of that commit's roster read twelve guard rows. amphora_mark_wreck was seated on this same day, hours before my reading, and it builds all three -- so it is the ninth builder and the sixteenth guard. The word eight went stale on the same day the digit gate landed, in the same room, two paragraphs from the gate.
think That is my own row %638 refuted by its own room. Its closing clause let a word-spelled number walk free since a spelled number cannot go stale in silence. It can, and one had. The lesson is not about words versus digits: a gate's exemption is a claim like any other, and mine was reasoned rather than measured.
think Before writing the reading I measured whether a gate at zero would be honest, because a wall that reds on ordinary work is a wall somebody turns off. The same door carries three more modules in a sentence that enumerates what it counts and is self-checking. So the reading is REPORTED, never gated -- and the witness asserts the field is PRESENT rather than zero, since a door that stopped answering and a door with nothing to report are two different facts.
obs The nouns are the four this instrument itself measures -- line, module, guard, witness -- so the reading never reaches a number it could not check. A word character after the noun ends the match and a letter before the number ends it, so eight guardrails and someone-line walk free, both proven in the control from the failing side.
obs Against myself, twice. My wait loop read pgrep -f standing_equipment_run, which matches a command line rather than a directory, so on a pier of eight ships it can never go quiet -- the %541/%628 family in a new verb. fleet_call.sh answers the signal question and nothing answers the wait one. I only ever READ, so no peer was touched; yet for half an hour my elapsed-time readings were grain-bakery's clock rather than my own, and I only found out by resolving /proc/<pid>/cwd. The cure is one line: wait on your own PID.
obs The row is born on a shelf because the pin still reads pin_headroom=24, rows_that_fit=0, pin_deadlocked=1 -- the same deadlock %638 recorded three hours earlier, so the two rows sit side by side. the number came off the anointed spine, which already held %639, and is cited by stamp until the spine binds it; the local monotone gap closes on the rebase, which is the derived spine working rather than failing.
